  "raw_response": {
    "answer": "For remote work, a temporary change of work location within the same country for fewer than 15 business days can be approved by the employee's manager without needing People Operations review. However, longer temporary changes or any work outside Canada or the United States require People Operations review due to tax, employment, and security implications, and such requests are considered ambiguous until reviewed. Regarding security rules for personal laptops, personal devices may be used for limited work access only if enrolled in approved mobile device management or accessed through approved browser-based tools. Personal devices must have a passcode, a supported operating system, and automatic lock enabled. Restricted data must not be downloaded to personal devices, and confidential data should only be accessed through approved company systems. Remote work must follow the Device and BYOD Security Policy and the Data Classification and Handling Policy, ensuring confidential and restricted data are accessed only on approved devices using company-approved tools.",
